onse handler that segments, aggregates, and classifies responses to distinguish human answers from voicemail, firing events accordingly."}, {"name": "TTSGate", "description": "A gate that buffers TTS frames until voicemail classification decision is made, then either releases or discards the buffered frames."}, {"name": "VoicemailDetector", "description": "Main class implementing a parallel pipeline for real-time voicemail detection in outbound calls, combining classification, gating, and event management."}], "methods": [{"name": "None _validate_prompt(self, prompt: str)", "description": "Validates that custom prompts instruct the LLM to respond with specific keywords for classification.", "scope": "VoicemailDetector", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "\"VoicemailDetector\" detector(self)", "description": "Returns the detector pipeline instance, meant for placement after speech-to-text in the main call pipeline.", "scope": "VoicemailDetector", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "TTSGate gate(self)", "description": "Returns the TTS gating processor for placement after TTS output.", "scope": "VoicemailDetector", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "add_event_handler(self, event_name: str, handler)", "description": "Allows registration of custom event handlers for voicemail detection events.", "scope": "VoicemailDetector", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "__init__( self, *, gate_notifier: BaseNotifier, conversation_notifier: BaseNotifier, voicemail_notifier: BaseNotifier, voicemail_response_delay: float, )", "scope": "ClassificationProcessor", "scopeKind": "class", "description": "unavailable"}, {"name": "__init__( self, *, llm: LLMService, voicemail_response_delay: float = 2.0, custom_system_prompt: Optional[str] = None, )", "scope": "VoicemailDetector", "scopeKind": "class", "description": "unavailable"}, {"name": "__init__(self, conversation_notifier: BaseNotifier, voicemail_notifier: BaseNotifier)", "scope": "TTSGate", "scopeKind": "class", "description": "unavailable"}, 